   "A": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to continuing the authority of the department of environmental conservation to adopt management regulations for deer and bear; and to amend chapter 600 of the laws of 1993, amending the environmental conservation law relating to the management of bear, in relation to the effectiveness of such chapter",
    "basePrintNo": "S5332",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5332-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §13, Chap 600 of 1993; amd §§11-0903 & 11-913, En Con L",
    "lawSection": "Environmental Conservation Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5332A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend the environmental conservation law, in relation to continuing\nthe authority of the department of environmental conservation to adopt\nmanagement regulations for deer and bear; and\nto amend chapter 600 of the laws of 1993, amending the environmental\nconservation law relating to the management of bear, in relation to the\neffectiveness of such chapter\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\nTo extend the law allowing for\nhunting of deer and bear until October 1, 2015.\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\nExtends the law allowing for hunting\nof deer and bear until October 1, 2015 from October 1, 2011.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nThis legislation is necessary to ensure that hunting of\ndeer bear within New York is legal for the period of time between\nOctober 1, 2011 and October 1, 2015.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
